cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use MiraProt in your research, please cite both the MiraProt software
  release used for your analysis and the associated publication listed under
  preferred-citation.

title: "MiraProt"

type: software

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-09-02"

authors:
  - family-names: "Schmalen"
    given-names: "Adrian"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2462-2675"

abstract: >-
  MiraProt is a modular R Shiny-based platform for integrated downstream
  analysis of processed protein-level proteomics data. It combines
  metadata-aware data preparation with differential abundance analysis,
  dimensionality reduction, functional enrichment and gene set enrichment
  analysis, protein interaction analysis, protein set comparison, and
  visualization within a connected interactive workflow. By retaining
  structured metadata across analysis steps, MiraProt facilitates consistent
  reuse of prepared datasets and reduces repeated restructuring and manual
  transfer of intermediate results between separate tools.

repository-code: "https://github.com/AdSchmalen/MiraProt"

license: MIT

doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22110860"

keywords:
  - "proteomics"
  - "R Shiny"
  - "downstream proteomics analysis"
  - "differential abundance"
  - "functional enrichment"
  - "gene set enrichment analysis"
  - "protein interaction analysis"
  - "data visualization"
  - "research software"
  - "metadata-aware data analysis"

